a lot of people think that the first  week of college you're finally an adult  and you have  everything under control but the reality  is first week of college  can be a mess  i thought college was going to be like  the miley cyrus movie lol  and so i just thought it was sororities  all the time having fun having  houses and partying all the time moving  to new york i thought college was gonna  be  like the movies where you know you're  going out with your girlfriends every  night  you're getting drinks you're you're  meeting new people but definitely being  a freshman it was  much different obviously i did not have  a lot of money so it was a lot of like a  lot of ramen noodles a lot of just  buckling down  in the beginning before like you really  find your footing in the city  another aspect of getting comfortable  with college is dorm life  it was a big transition going from a  small room at home by myself to sharing  rooms but i didn't really  expect for what we call the great bone  flood to happen  one night after i hit the gym i came  home  and i came and the entire building was  raining  and i was very confused to why it was  raining  inside found out on the 13th floor of my  building  somebody clogged a toilet where it led  to an explosion of the pipes in the  building  from floor 13 down everybody's stuff was  kind of ruined  this was kind of scary i was like this  is crazy because it was like a lot of  water  they rushed us to grab all our  belongings meaning i had to run 14  floors because i lived in the 14th floor  through poop water  to grab my stuff and my roommate and  dash out the building  it was kind of like a sour smell like  what you would expect i would say  new york city subway esque smell your  first day of college can be a little  hectic that's when you move into your  dorm you get to meet your new roommates  your ra  and the people in your dorm building you  may have to do a few orientation  activities like icebreakers and getting  to know new people  but once the night time hits that's when  the fun begins there's usually different  parties you can go to to celebrate your  first day of college and you get to make  new friends  second day is pretty more relaxed you  get to do whatever you want classes  haven't started yet so  walk to the dining halls if there's  multiple dining halls if you go to a  bear campus  maybe find some food that you like if  there's food that you like in  college campus dining halls on your  third day of college you're going to  start making friends with people in your  dorm with people  in your suite and you're going to see if  you guys connect  and you're going to want to like go to  dunkin grab some coffee or  maybe like want to go to a cute brunch  spot and like get to know each other  talk about classes that you share you're  going to be brushing off those social  skills learning how to  make friends again in a different  environment take it day by day so your  fourth day is when you get a chance to  buy any other materials you'll need for  the next week for example you can buy  different school supplies like your  backpacks your notebooks and just make  sure you're prepared with any textbooks  you may need for  class next week on day five aka the end  of the week  you might have felt comfortable might be  branching out going to some  organizations to sign up and whatever  your interest is  you might have class you might not have  class just depending on what schedule  you have  you'll probably sit in class and be a  little anxious to meet friends and meet  people you could probably connect with  to study later on  these are the days that most parties  happen sadly my  school was not a very party-heavy campus  they had parties but i didn't really  know about them at the time an important  aspect of college  is getting to know your roommates i  definitely uh got to know mine a little  more  during my first week of college i lived  with three  roommates we were all getting to know  each other you know the first week my  roommates and i  we went out the night before we're  having a great time  i assumed everyone was you know tucked  in their beds the next day everyone's  fine it was the weekend  around like three in the afternoon i  hear this knock on the door  and it sounds quite urgent and i just  assume it's one of my roommates who you  know got locked out i'm like okay i'll  get up i'll  i'll be the one that has to get up and  open the door i open the door  there's three cops already outside my  door i see two more down the hallway and  i see like the red lights flashing you  know  outside the farther i look there's more  piling in so i'm like okay  what's what's going on and so they asked  me they're like oh hey  do you know this person naming one of my  roommates and i'm like yeah  i do know them why what's up they're  asking me oh have you have you seen them  with a weapon any  weapons inside the apartment and i'm  like no not that i know of i haven't  seen anything with my  own two eyeballs and they're like yeah  we need to talk to them we need to talk  to them right now  and so my sister and i we go outside and  we're like we're waiting there  my heart is pounding you know i just  moved to new york city for the first  time  i have no idea what's going on i'm like  is this normal is this the adorable  saturday afternoon in new york city  eventually they're done talking to our  roommate  which i'm like great please let me back  inside my apartment ask my roommate i'm  like okay  what what what was that what was going  on there my roommate proceeds to tell me  their mom called the cops on them  because she thought they stole something  from her  i don't know why they needed that many  cops though for such a very small thing  but i guess it was super intense and  they were totally calm about it didn't  blink an eye and i'm like okay i guess  this you know  normal day and you're like safe to say  our roommate dinner that week  was quite awkward another important  aspect of college are the parties my  first week of college my housemates and  i decided to throw a house party we just  wanted to have  a small party but this party went  nothing like plans  some drunk girls thought it'd be a great  idea to throw some glass bottles into  our washing machine  and run the machine and when we tried to  track them down they got lost throughout  the house  this wasn't our only problem some frat  guys from the college down the street  broke into our house pulled out some  random matches from our basements  and jumped off our roof afterwards they  ran through the back  and broke our fence my housemates and i  started freaking out because we'd have  to pay for that fence  and one of my housemates got so angry he  picked up a baseball bat and decided to  go after them at that point  everyone at the party pulls out their  cell phones and starts recording because  they are ready to see a fight my  housemate gets angry and turns around  and almost swings the bat at one of them  until i catch the baseball bat  and take it away from him at that point  we all decide it's time for the party to  be over  so we send everyone home early and that  was my first rager  in my first week of college you know  sometimes in college you might  meet new friends or get your stuff  ruined by  dirty sewage water but it's college and  it's all about the experience you know  so your first week of college may not be  what you expected but  i would not change those experiences for  the world i cherish those and i would  not  be who i am today without those  experiences college can be a really  crazy experience  people may jump off your roof and  destroy your college house  but at the end of the day it was a great  experience it's something that i'll  always look at fondly and it's truly the  best years of your life i wouldn't  change a thing  you

